    "Description": "Red Hat JBoss Enterprise Application Platform 8 is a platform for Java\napplications based on the WildFly application runtime.\n\nThis asynchronous patch is an update for Red Hat JBoss Enterprise Application\nPlatform 8.1. See Release Notes for information about the most significant bug\nfixes and enhancements included in this release.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* bcjmail-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle for Java: Integrity compromise due to insufficient tag-length enforcement in CMS AuthEnvelopedData decryption. [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-12802)\n\n* bcpg-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle for Java: Integrity compromise due to insufficient tag-length enforcement in CMS AuthEnvelopedData decryption. [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-12802)\n\n* bcutil-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle for Java: Integrity compromise due to insufficient tag-length enforcement in CMS AuthEnvelopedData decryption. [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-12802)\n\n* bcpkix-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle for Java: Integrity compromise due to insufficient tag-length enforcement in CMS AuthEnvelopedData decryption. [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-12802)\n\n* bcjmail-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle for Java: Denial of Service via OER parser unbounded recursion [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-59645)\n\n* bcpg-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle for Java: Denial of Service via OER parser unbounded recursion [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-59645)\n\n* bcutil-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle for Java: Denial of Service via OER parser unbounded recursion [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-59645)\n\n* bcpkix-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle for Java: Denial of Service via OER parser unbounded recursion [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-59645)\n\n* bcprov-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle for Java: Denial of Service via OER parser unbounded recursion [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-59645)\n\n* bcprov-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle for Java: Integrity compromise due to insufficient tag-length enforcement in CMS AuthEnvelopedData decryption. [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-12802)\n\n* bcjmail-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle for Java: Cryptographic signature bypass [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-59639)\n\n* bcpg-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle for Java: Cryptographic signature bypass [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-59639)\n\n* bcpkix-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle for Java: Cryptographic signature bypass [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-59639)\n\n* bcprov-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle for Java: Cryptographic signature bypass [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-59639)\n\n* bcjmail-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle for Java: Data integrity bypass due to improper cryptographic binding in CMS AuthenticatedData [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-59642)\n\n* bcpg-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle for Java: Data integrity bypass due to improper cryptographic binding in CMS AuthenticatedData [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-59642)\n\n* bcutil-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle for Java: Data integrity bypass due to improper cryptographic binding in CMS AuthenticatedData [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-59642)\n\n* bcpkix-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle for Java: Data integrity bypass due to improper cryptographic binding in CMS AuthenticatedData [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-59642)\n\n* bcprov-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle for Java: Data integrity bypass due to improper cryptographic binding in CMS AuthenticatedData [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-59642)\n\n* bcjmail-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle for Java: Denial of Service via unbounded HSS public-key level count [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-58060)\n\n* bcpg-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle for Java: Denial of Service via unbounded HSS public-key level count [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-58060)\n\n* bcutil-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle for Java: Denial of Service via unbounded HSS public-key level count [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-58060)\n\n* bcpkix-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle for Java: Denial of Service via unbounded HSS public-key level count [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-58060)\n\n* bcprov-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle for Java: Denial of Service via unbounded HSS public-key level count [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-58060)\n\n* bcpg-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle for Java: Integrity bypass in CCM-family modes [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-58061)\n\n* bcprov-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle for Java: Integrity bypass in CCM-family modes [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-58061)\n\n* sshd-core: Apache MINA SSHD: Asynchronous authentication can bypass signature verification [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-77185)\n\n* jackson-core: jackson-core: Denial of Service via excessively long JSON property names [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-68498)\n\n* bcutil-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle: Certificate validation bypass via missing name constraint checks [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-71889)\n\n* bcjmail-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle: Certificate validation bypass via missing name constraint checks [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-71889)\n\n* bcpg-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle: Certificate validation bypass via missing name constraint checks [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-71889)\n\n* bcprov-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle: Certificate validation bypass via missing name constraint checks [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-71889)\n\n* bcpkix-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle: Certificate validation bypass via missing name constraint checks [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-71889)\n\n* jackson-core: Jackson-core: Denial of Service via unbounded StringBuilder growth during malformed token processing [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-89425)\n\n* jackson-databind: Jackson-databind: Denial of Service via quadratic forward-reference completion [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-91777)\n\n* bcpg-jdk18on: Bouncy Castle: Signature misattribution via missing subkey cross-certification validation [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-71887)\n\n* sshd-core: Apache MINA SSHD: Authentication bypass via duplicate public key presentation [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-93994)\n\n* xmlschema-core: Apache XMLSchema: Denial of Service (DoS) via deeply nested schema structures [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-102496)\n\n* xmlschema-core: Apache XMLSchema: Denial of Service via unbounded recursion during schema parsing [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-102495)\n\n* jackson-core: Jackson-core: Denial of Service via regular expression backtracking [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-89407)\n\n* neethi: Neethi: Denial of Service via crafted WS-Policy documents [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-91866)\n\n* neethi: Apache Neethi: Denial of Service via crafted WS-Policy documents [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-91865)\n\n* neethi: Apache Neethi: Denial of Service via uncontrolled recursion in WS-Policy document parsing [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-91863)\n\n* neethi: Apache Neethi: Denial of Service via crafted WS-Policy documents [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-91864)\n\n* wildfly-server: wildfly: RBAC bypass in WildFly deployment-operation handlers leads to privilege escalation [eap-8.1.z] (CVE-2026-12977)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS\nscore, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s)\nlisted in the References section.",
